{
  "spec": "rogue-subtlety",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Subtlety at 60, hand-curated from simmed candidates (design/reviews/2026-10-07-rogue-curation.md). The stealth opener (Stealth, Premeditation, Ambush) is unchanged. In the fight, Hemorrhage builds and keeps its Rupture-amplifying debuff up, Ghostly Strike goes on cooldown, Rupture is the main finisher whenever it has lapsed, and Eviscerate and Slice and Dice spend the combo points that build while it runs. Every rank named here is checked against this build's own spellconst. 2026-10-31 (theorycraft audit fixes): Ambush moves from one second before the pull to the pull itself. The engine records no damage dealt before the pull, so the -1 s Ambush spent 60 Energy and its hit counted for nothing; at 0 s the rogue is still stealthed and the hit counts. 2026-11-02 guide rewrite: Garrote replaces Ambush after Premeditation (Initiative adds the fourth point; a bleed ignores the unsundered armor at the pull), +1.0% raid 60.",
  "expected_idle": [
    {
      "id": 11294,
      "reason": "Sinister Strike is gated `not spellIsKnown(Hemorrhage/16511)`, the fallback builder for a bare build below Hemorrhage's talent row (Subtlety tier 4). At every level this ladder's own zero_casts check flags it, the truncated talent build has already spent points on Hemorrhage, so the gate correctly keeps Sinister Strike idle and lets Hemorrhage claim the builder slot instead -- the fallback yielding as designed, not a defect."
    },
    {
      "id": 11300,
      "reason": "Eviscerate and Slice and Dice only spend combo points built while Rupture is running. On the ladder's bare rungs (levels 10 to 50) energy is scarce enough that every set of combo points goes straight into Rupture, which is cast again as soon as it ends, so no points are left for Eviscerate (Slice and Dice is cast from level 20); at level 60, with the full talent build, Eviscerate is cast."
    },
    {
      "id": 6774,
      "reason": "Same as Eviscerate above: at level 20 (and, when it is learned, 30) no combo points are left over while Rupture is running."
    }
  ],
  "engineering_notes": {
    "5": "Fix round: the ladder's bare build has zero points in Hemorrhage below the level its tier is reachable (tier 4 of the Subtlety tree), leaving no combo-point builder at all -- the same auraIsKnown/spellIsKnown gate shape mage-fire uses for Improved Scorch (12873).",
    "2": "Previously starved entirely: Slice and Dice used to sit here instead, re-applying itself at currentComboPoints >= 1 with no floor, so it looped at 1-3 combo points forever and this line never saw five combo points."
  },
